==Notes==
* The [[transformation]] abilities of most Beast fruits either provide high defense, mobility, or high healing, all of which are very helpful for surviving heavy damage that can be sustained during [[Raids]].
* [[Dragon]] has a transformation that buffs all of its moves, hitting most opponents with the fruit's large attack hitbox.
* [[Buddha]] has a big melee hitbox and when awakened, can pretty much solo any [[Raids|raid]] with the right build and the right stats. 
* [[Phoenix]] has a heal ability that can be extremely useful in raids.
* When transformed, [[Mammoth]] has an ability that can endlessly damage enemies.
* Some Beast fruits (such as [[Tiger]]) have speed buffs.
* Many beast fruits (such as [[Dragon]]) have high damage reduction whilst transformed.
* [[Yeti]] is a good team-based fruit in sea events by creating ice platforms for teammates to stand on.
* [[Eagle]] allows the user to wield weapons while flying which is useful for aerial combat.

==Trivia==
* Despite [[Venom]], [[Rubber]], and [[Diamond]] having a transformation, they are currently considered [[Natural]] fruits. [[Gas]] is currently an [[Elemental]] fruit, despite it having a transformation.
* There are currently no {{Common}} or {{Rare}} Beast fruits in the game.
* Every beast fruit except [[Eagle]] has a full transformation.
** However, the game considers Eagle's flight mode as a transformation.
* Only 2 Beast-type fruits have an awakening, those fruits being [[Phoenix]] and [[Buddha]].
* [[Eagle]] and [[Tiger]] are the only beast types that take after a real present-day animal. Every other beast type either take on a mythical being or a slightly altered extinct animal.
* [[Spider]] is not a beast fruit. Despite the fact that it has changed its name, it has not changed its type: it is a [[Natural]] fruit. It is also because that the [[Spider]] fruit allows the user to control strings instead of turning them into a spider (because it used to be the String Fruit).
* [[Mammoth]] and [[T-Rex]] cost the same amount of [[Money]] and have the same Permanent Value. [[Tiger]] and [[Yeti]] now share these too.
* [[Eagle]] is currently the cheapest and least rare of all the Beast-type fruits in the game.
* [[Dragon]] is the most expensive Beast-type [[Blox Fruit]], costing {{Money|15,000,000}}, as well as being the most expensive in general. 
* [[Buddha]] is the only Beast fruit that needs to have its transformation active to be able to use its moves.
* Awakened [[Buddha]], [[Phoenix]], [[T-Rex]] and [[Dragon]] are the only [[Beast]] fruits to have a transformation move that is not named "[[Transformations|Transformation]]".
* There are currently 8 beast fruits that have an M1 (left click), these fruits are: [[Dragon]], [[Kitsune]], [[Yeti]], [[Tiger]], [[T-Rex]], [[Mammoth]], Awakened [[Phoenix]] and [[Eagle]].
* Many of the Beast fruits do not allow the user to use their [[Fighting Styles]], [[Swords]] or [[Guns]] while transformed except for [[Buddha]] and [[Dragon]] (Hybrid).
** [[Eagle]] technically does not have a transformation, but the user is able to yield weapons while flying.
* As of {{Update|29}}, [[Eagle]], [[Dragon]] and [[Kitsune|Kitsune's]] [[Empyrean]] mutation are the only beast fruits that have usable [[skins]].
* As of {{Update|29}}, [[Tiger]], [[Kitsune]], and [[Yeti]] are the only fruits to have a mutation, those being [[Werewolf]], [[Empyrean]], and [[Fiend]] respectively.
* Beast have the lowest amount of [[Blox Fruits]], having a total of 9 fruits, Elemental having 11 fruits, and [[Natural]] having 22 fruits.
* [[Buddha]] is the only Beast fruit that does not transform into an animal, but a mythical being. 
* If the user enables [[Aura]] while in a Beast transformation (except for [[Buddha]] and [[Eagle]]) and then untransformed, the user will not have the [[Aura]] glow effect, But the player will have the [[Aura]] buffs and the glow effects if the player uses a [[Swords|Sword]] or a [[Guns|Gun]]. (Only been tested with [[T-Rex]], Doesn't work with [[Buddha]], unknown if this works with other beast transformations)
* As of [[Updates/28|Update 28]], [[Dragon]] and [[Tiger]] are the only Beast-type fruits to have two different [[transformations]]. (Western and Eastern, and Blazing Form respectively.) 

